{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"nonmystic-topiary-toadfish","creation_channel":"cli","description":"# J11 — Prove bidirectional reconciliation live, against a realistic store\n\n## Why this exists\n\nEpic e369's headline AC is:\n\n> [operator-attested] rebar reconciles bidirectionally against the Dockerized Jira instance ... at\n> least one issue created in DC appears in the local store after an inbound pass, and one local edit\n> appears on the DC issue after an outbound pass, with zero unhandled exceptions\n\nIt is NOT met, and the way it failed is instructive. CI run 30637886718 reported:\n\n    invariants: scanned=0 filed=0\n    OK: steady-state pass converged\n    RECON: outbound_differ total=0   inbound_differ total=0\n\n**Scanned zero.** The pass converged because there was nothing to reconcile. That proves the\nreconciler runs cleanly against an EMPTY instance — it does not prove data moves. On an empty store\n'converged' and 'works' are indistinguishable, and only one of them is the criterion. Closing the epic\non that output would have been the fifth instance in this epic of green-but-broken.\n\nThe existing live module builds its store with the `rebar_repo` fixture: `rebar.init_repo()` on an\nempty temp dir. Nothing to sync, so nothing syncs.\n\n## Approach\n\nRun the live verification against a COPY OF THIS PROJECT'S ACTUAL TICKET STORE, so the pass sees\nrealistic volume, ticket shapes, link graphs, comment histories and field values — the conditions that\nsurface pagination, ordering and field-mapping defects an empty store cannot.\n\n### Isolation is the first requirement, not an afterthought\n\nrebar AUTO-COMMITS and AUTO-PUSHES ticket events to `sync.remote`. A copy of this project's store that\nretained its configuration could push test mutations back at the real project. Defence in depth, in\npriority order:\n\n1. **A SEPARATE REPO WITH NO REMOTES — the primary mechanism.** The CI job `git init`s a fresh repo and\n   copies the ticket-store content in. It never adds `origin`. There is then physically nowhere to\n   push, independent of any config or env value. This is stronger than a flag because it cannot be\n   defeated by a mis-read setting.\n2. `REBAR_SYNC_PUSH=off` as a second, independent layer (`sync.push` accepts `always|async|off`;\n   the env override is authoritative).\n3. The reconciler config points ONLY at the harness (`reconciler.base_url` = the container). No Cloud\n   credentials are present in the job environment at all — no `JIRA_URL`, no `JIRA_API_TOKEN`, no\n   `acli` auth — so the Cloud path cannot be driven even by accident.\n4. **The isolation is ASSERTED, not assumed.** A test fails the job if `git remote` returns anything in\n   the working repo, or if `sync.remote` resolves to a non-empty value. Safety that is not tested is\n   an intention.\n\n### The DC-side mutation suite\n\nComprehensive mutations applied to the HARNESS instance (never a real Jira), each asserted to\nround-trip, so the bridge is exercised rather than merely started:\n\n* **inbound (DC -> local):** create issue; edit summary; edit description; transition status; add\n  label; remove label; add comment; edit comment; assign; unassign; create issue link; delete issue\n  link; set sub-task parent; clear parent; delete issue (absence probe).\n* **outbound (local -> DC):** the mirror set, driven by local ticket edits.\n* **volume:** enough issues to force MULTIPLE pagination pages, since the DC page cap is\n  server-configurable and truncation is silent (`get_parent_map` had exactly this defect).\n* **idempotence:** an immediately repeated pass after each direction writes nothing.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `.github/workflows/external-integration.yml` — the `jira-dc-harness` job gains the store-copy step\n  (fresh `git init`, no remote) and the isolation assertions.\n- `tests/external/live_jira_dc/` — the mutation suite and its fixtures; a `dc_mutations` helper that\n  applies each DC-side change through the real transport.\n- `tests/external/live_jira_dc/README.md` — document the isolation contract and WHY (auto-push).\n\n**NOT in scope:** any change that could write to this project's Jira or its tickets branch.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] the working repo in CI has NO git remote, asserted by a test that FAILS the job otherwise —\n      this is the primary isolation and it must be verified, not assumed\n- [ ] `REBAR_SYNC_PUSH=off` and an empty `sync.remote` are both asserted in the same test\n- [ ] no Cloud credential is present in the job environment, asserted by test\n- [ ] the store under test is a COPY of this project's real ticket store, and the pass reports\n      `scanned` > 0 — the specific failure that made the previous run meaningless\n- [ ] [operator-attested] an issue created in DC appears in the local store after an inbound pass\n- [ ] [operator-attested] a local edit appears on the DC issue after an outbound pass\n- [ ] every mutation in the suite above round-trips, each asserted individually rather than by an\n      aggregate 'converged' line\n- [ ] a repeated pass after each direction writes nothing (idempotence)\n- [ ] the run exercises MULTIPLE pagination pages, so silent truncation cannot pass\n- [ ] zero unhandled exceptions, asserted on the reconciler subprocess streams\n- [ ] this project's live Jira is untouched: the suite never resolves a non-harness base URL,\n      asserted by test","id":"5200-e04e-246e-4aae","parent_id":"e369-a449-4773-48fb","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"story","title":"J11 — prove the epic's headline live: real store copy, comprehensive DC mutations, hard isolation"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785510469978033001,"uuid":"9133d75a-c87c-440c-a3f9-ae46a34c6f4d"}